# The distribution payload is ASSEMBLED by scripts/build-getff-dist.sh from the repo root
# (git-tracked files only) and is never committed here — the committed artefact is
# MANIFEST.sha256, and `build-getff-dist.sh --check` is the drift gate. Every copied
# top-level path is named explicitly (no `*`), so a new payload root has to be added in
# three places on purpose: the assembler's PAYLOAD list, package.json `files`, and here.
/install.sh
/setup
/setup.d/
/agents/
/skills/
/templates/
/.claude/
/.prettierrc.json
/packages/
/scripts/
/*.tgz
